sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: An agent shops on a merchant website with a Visa card: TAP browsing and payer signatures, a VIC token, verification at the CDN
  accDescr: Sequence diagram: An agent shops on a merchant website with a Visa card: TAP browsing and payer signatures, a VIC token, verification at the CDN. 7 participants: Consumer, AI agent (Agent Provider), Visa Intelligent Commerce, CDN (Site Protection Provider), Visa key store, Merchant website, and Acquirer, Visa network and issuer. 16 steps, 13 crossing a trust boundary, 11 failure branches. Based on several protocols TAP spec, unversioned (read 2026-10-11, rechecked 2026-10-19) VIC API client in visa/ai (2026-09-30) (2025-10-14). Step 1: Consumer to AI agent (Agent Provider): Ask the agent to buy an item. Step 2: AI agent (Agent Provider) to Visa Intelligent Commerce: POST /vacp/v1/cards (card enrollment). This step crosses a trust boundary. If Step-up verification or passkey setup fails: The card is not enabled for the agent, and no purchase instruction can be created. Step 3: AI agent (Agent Provider) to CDN (Site Protection Provider): GET product page, signed with tag agent-browser-auth. This step crosses a trust boundary. If A checkout enabler or proxy strips the signature headers: The request arrives untagged and is treated as an unknown bot. Step 4: CDN (Site Protection Provider) to Visa key store: Fetch the key for keyid. This step crosses a trust boundary. If No key for keyid, or the key has expired: Block the request TAP has no revocation list or key status endpoint. Step 5: CDN (Site Protection Provider) to CDN (Site Protection Provider): Verify tag, fields, window, nonce and signature. If Neither agent-browser-auth nor agent-payer-auth in Signature-Input: Not signed by a trusted agent block or apply ordinary bot policy. If Missing field, window over 8 minutes, reused nonce or failed signature: Block the request. Step 6: CDN (Site Protection Provider) to Merchant website: Forward as a verified browsing agent. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 7: Merchant website to AI agent (Agent Provider): 200 product page with final cost. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 8: Consumer to AI agent (Agent Provider): Authenticate the purchase instruction with a passkey. This step crosses a trust boundary. If The consumer declines or the passkey check fails: No instruction is created and no credentials can be retrieved nothing is charged. Step 9: AI agent (Agent Provider) to Visa Intelligent Commerce: POST /vacp/v1/instructions (Payment Instruction with the authentication result). This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 10: AI agent (Agent Provider) to Visa Intelligent Commerce: POST /vacp/v1/instructions/ instructionId /credentials. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 11: AI agent (Agent Provider) to CDN (Site Protection Provider): POST checkout, signed with tag agent-payer-auth, with agenticConsumer and agenticPaymentContainer. This step crosses a trust boundary. If The body is altered in transit: The header signature still verifies only the body object signatures can catch it. Step 12: CDN (Site Protection Provider) to Merchant website: Verify the payer signature at the edge, forward. This step crosses a trust boundary. If The agent signed the checkout before the passkey approval and the 8-minute window ran out: Block the agent signs a fresh request with a new nonce. Step 13: Merchant website to Merchant website: Verify the body objects and the credential hash. If Payment container fields missing, nonce mismatch or bad signature: Should not be used for payment. If The merchant's hash of the key-entered card data differs from the payment credential hash: The specification says the merchant should decline. Step 14: Merchant website to Acquirer, Visa network and issuer: Authorize the card payment. This step crosses a trust boundary. If The issuer declines: An ordinary card decline TAP has no role. Step 15: Merchant website to AI agent (Agent Provider): Order confirmation. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 16: AI agent (Agent Provider) to Visa Intelligent Commerce: POST /vacp/v1/instructions/ instructionId /confirmations. This step crosses a trust boundary.
  autonumber
  participant p_user as Consumer
  participant p_agent as AI agent (Agent Provider)
  participant p_vic as Visa Intelligent Commerce
  participant p_cdn as CDN (Site Protection Provider)
  participant p_keystore as Visa key store
  participant p_merchant as Merchant website
  participant p_acquirer as Acquirer, Visa network and issuer
  p_user->>p_agent: Ask the agent to buy an item
  alt Expected path
    p_agent->>p_vic: POST /vacp/v1/cards (card enrollment)
    Note over p_agent,p_vic: Crosses a trust boundary
  else Step-up verification or passkey setup fails
    Note over p_agent,p_vic: The card is not enabled for the agent, and<br/>no purchase instruction can be created.
  end
  alt Expected path
    p_agent->>p_cdn: GET product page, signed with tag agent-browser-auth
    Note over p_agent,p_cdn: Crosses a trust boundary
  else A checkout enabler or proxy strips the signature headers
    Note over p_agent,p_cdn: The request arrives untagged and is treated as an unknown bot.
  end
  alt Expected path
    p_cdn->>p_keystore: Fetch the key for keyid
    Note over p_cdn,p_keystore: Crosses a trust boundary
  else No key for keyid, or the key has expired
    Note over p_cdn,p_keystore: Block the request#59; TAP has no<br/>revocation list or key status endpoint.
  end
  alt Expected path
    p_cdn->>p_cdn: Verify tag, fields, window, nonce and signature
  else Neither agent-browser-auth nor agent-payer-auth in Signature-Input
    Note over p_cdn: Not signed by a trusted agent#59;<br/>block or apply ordinary bot policy.
  else Missing field, window over 8 minutes, reused nonce or failed signature
    Note over p_cdn: Block the request.
  end
  p_cdn->>p_merchant: Forward as a verified browsing agent
  Note over p_cdn,p_merchant: Crosses a trust boundary
  p_merchant-->>p_agent: 200 product page with final cost
  Note over p_merchant,p_agent: Crosses a trust boundary
  alt Expected path
    p_user->>p_agent: Authenticate the purchase instruction with a passkey
    Note over p_user,p_agent: Crosses a trust boundary
  else The consumer declines or the passkey check fails
    Note over p_user,p_agent: No instruction is created and no credentials<br/>can be retrieved#59; nothing is charged.
  end
  p_agent->>p_vic: POST /vacp/v1/instructions (Payment<br/>Instruction with the authentication result)
  Note over p_agent,p_vic: Crosses a trust boundary
  p_agent->>p_vic: POST<br/>/vacp/v1/instructions/#123;instructionId#125;/credentials
  Note over p_agent,p_vic: Crosses a trust boundary
  alt Expected path
    p_agent->>p_cdn: POST checkout, signed with tag agent-payer-auth,<br/>with agenticConsumer and agenticPaymentContainer
    Note over p_agent,p_cdn: Crosses a trust boundary
  else The body is altered in transit
    Note over p_agent,p_cdn: The header signature still verifies#59; only<br/>the body object signatures can catch it.
  end
  alt Expected path
    p_cdn->>p_merchant: Verify the payer signature at the edge, forward
    Note over p_cdn,p_merchant: Crosses a trust boundary
  else The agent signed the checkout before the passkey approval and the 8-minute window ran out
    Note over p_cdn,p_merchant: Block#59; the agent signs a fresh request with a new nonce.
  end
  alt Expected path
    p_merchant->>p_merchant: Verify the body objects and the credential hash
  else Payment container fields missing, nonce mismatch or bad signature
    Note over p_merchant: Should not be used for payment.
  else The merchant#39;s hash of the key-entered card data differs from the payment credential hash
    Note over p_merchant: The specification says the merchant should decline.
  end
  alt Expected path
    p_merchant->>p_acquirer: Authorize the card payment
    Note over p_merchant,p_acquirer: Crosses a trust boundary
  else The issuer declines
    Note over p_merchant,p_acquirer: An ordinary card decline#59; TAP has no role.
  end
  p_merchant->>p_agent: Order confirmation
  Note over p_merchant,p_agent: Crosses a trust boundary
  p_agent->>p_vic: POST<br/>/vacp/v1/instructions/#123;instructionId#125;/confirmations
  Note over p_agent,p_vic: Crosses a trust boundary
